,title,link,text,language,family
0,Bolyu | Ethnologue Free,https://www.ethnologue.com/language/ply/?cf=1&token=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9..vEjtDgudbN0GD_d1RrmbjXdc5x48cEYR6_-66wyQzWQ,"Bolyu is an endangered indigenous language of China. It belongs to the Austro-Asiatic language family. Direct evidence is lacking, but the language is thought to be used as a first language by older adults only.",Bolyu,Austro-Asiatic
1,Bolyu — Grokipedia,https://grokipedia.com/page/bolyu,"The Bolyu language belongs to the Pakanic branch of the Austroasiatic phylum, forming a close linguistic pair with Bugan (also known as Pakan), as established through comparative reconstruction of Proto-Pakanic.",Bolyu,Austro-Asiatic
2,ABVD: Bolyu,https://abvd.eva.mpg.de/austronesian/language.php?id=960,"The Bolyu of Guangxi are officially classified as ethnic Gelao. Bolyu has many loanwords with Gelao; also, the Bolyu people may have originally migrated from western Guizhou in predominantly Gelao-speaking territories.",Bolyu,Austro-Asiatic
3,pmswiki-Lenga_bolyu-20200725.pdf : Wikipedia... : Internet Archive,https://archive.org/details/pmswiki-Lenga_bolyu-20200725.pdf,La lenga bolyu o Bolyu a fa part ed le lenghe Austro-Asiatiche e a I'e parla dzortut an Cin-a. Classlfica. IT. Ne schema ed classifica del Bolyu a peul esse: lenghe austro-asiatiche lenghe mon-khmer lenghe palyu.,Bolyu,Austro-Asiatic
4,Bolyu tone in Vietic perspective Jerold A. EDMONDSON Univ,http://sealang.net/sala/archives/pdf8/edmondson1996bolyu.pdf,"The Bolyu live in mixed communities with Miao and others in Longlin Various Nationalities Autonomous County Khmer groups. According to Hang (1989), there are also some Bolyu living just south of Longlin in Xilin County.",Bolyu,Austro-Asiatic
5,Bolyu language - Wikiwand,https://www.wikiwand.com/en/articles/Bolyu_language,"Bolyu is related to the Bugan language, forming the Pakanic branch along with it. In 1984, Bolyu was first studied by Liang Min of the Nationalities Research Institute in Beijing.",Bolyu,Austro-Asiatic
6,Austro-Asiatic Language Family - Structure & Dialects - MustGo,https://www-mustgo-com.nproxy.org/worldlanguages/austro-asiatic-language-family/,"The Austro-Asiatic language family consists of 169 languages spoken in Southeast Asia, in countries located between China and Indonesia. A few are spoken to the west of this area in the Nicobar Islands and in India. The austro– part of the name comes from the Latin word for ‘south.’",Bolyu,Austro-Asiatic
7,Le mot 'sang' en austroasiatique,https://shs.hal.science/halshs-00948583v1/document,les langues viet-muong méridionales et en bolyu. Cette dernière correspondance est de la plus haute importance pour comprendre un des aspects de la tonogenèse dans cette partie du monde.,Bolyu,Austro-Asiatic
8,Bolyu language and alphabet,https://omniglot.com/writing/bolyu.htm,"Bolyu is a member of the Pakanic branch of the Austroasiatic language family.Bolyu is also known as Baliu, Buliu, Lai, Lai Yu, Lailai, Paliu, Palju, Palyu, Polyu. It can be written with the Latin alphabet, although it rarely is written.",Bolyu,Austro-Asiatic
9,Bolyu | Languages and Nationalities of China,https://minzuyuyan.com/en/node/3836,"Language or Dialect Name (English). Bolyu.孟高棉语族 Austro-Asiatic, Mon-Khmer.",Bolyu,Austro-Asiatic
